Fixed path contraction with PLUMED
=================================

Build LAMMPS with the REPLICA and PLUMED packages and use an MPI-enabled
PLUMED kernel with ENSEMBLE support. Run from a writable copy of this folder:

  mpiexec -n 4 lmp -partition 4x1 -in in.pimd
  mpiexec -n 4 lmp -partition 4x1 -var ensemble npt -in in.pimd
  mpiexec -n 8 lmp -partition 4x2 -var contraction 0.0 -in in.pimd

The NPT variant uses the BZP barostat with an orthogonal simulation cell.

The default fixed contraction is 0.5. Values 0 and 1 give centroid-CV and
bead-mean-CV biases through the same PLUMED graph. The dynamics and bias
names are arbitrary fix IDs. The example uses reduced Lennard-Jones units.

The scalar f_bias reports the whole-path physical bias on the first bead
partition and zero on the others. f_dynamics[10] is the PIMD centroid-virial
pressure estimator. This short example demonstrates the interface; it is
not an equilibrium sampling or convergence test.
